{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.List","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.covariance_kernel_le_zero_of_le_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.covariance_kernel_le_zero_of_le_eight","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L402-L421","doc":"**The conjecture holds on `k ≤ 8`** — proved in Lean, not sampled.\n\n`kernelValue` is fully computable (a sum over `partsOf k`), so every\ninstance decides. Kernel evaluation only, **no `native_decide`**. This\nupgrades part of the \"verified `k ≤ 30` computationally\" above from an\nexternal Python check to a machine-checked statement.\n\nEvaluated further out: `k = 0,1,2` give `0`, and the value is strictly\nnegative from `k = 3` —\n`-4, -16, -320, -10400, -163520, -3224704, -106339296, -4722309120`\nat `k = 3…10`. So the §9 small-instance check finds nothing here: this is a\n**genuine open conjecture**, and the only survivor of the sweep in bean\n`qou-octr`, where eight sibling `sorry`s all turned out to be refutable.\n\nThe general case is real mathematics: `Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)³ · ω₃(λ) ≤ 0` carries\na *cubed* dimension, so it is not the Plancherel expectation of `ω₃` and\nthe standard `E_Planch[ω₃] = 0` identity does not reach it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.covariance_kernel_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.covariance_kernel_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L393-L400","doc":"**CONJECTURE (OPEN).** The covariance kernel `Cov_Planch(f^λ, Σ_□ c(□)²) ≤ 0`, in its\nelementary content form: for every `k`, `Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)³ (Σ_□c(□)² − C(k,2)) ≤ 0`. This is the sole\nopen input of the Δ_λ super-exponential growth bound (`WstdSuperExpBound.lean`, via the reduction\n`DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_T3_nonpos`). It is a Biane–Śniady / Kerov-CLT character-ratio\nanti-correlation; verified `k ≤ 30` computationally. Not proved.\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-07-18-deltalambda-covariance-kernel-frontier.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture.nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture.nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L391-L391","doc":"The covariance kernel value is non-positive for all k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L389-L389","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.CovarianceKernelConjecture","kind":"class","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L383-L391","doc":"**CONJECTURE (OPEN).** The covariance kernel `Cov_Planch(f^λ, Σ_□ c(□)²) ≤ 0`, in its\nelementary content form: for every `k`, `Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)³ (Σ_□c(□)² − C(k,2)) ≤ 0`. This is the sole\nopen input of the Δ_λ super-exponential growth bound (`WstdSuperExpBound.lean`, via the reduction\n`DeltaLambdaDReduction.D_of_T3_nonpos`). It is a Biane–Śniady / Kerov-CLT character-ratio\nanti-correlation; verified `k ≤ 30` computationally. Not proved.\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-07-18-deltalambda-covariance-kernel-frontier.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.M6_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.M6_pos","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L368-L381","doc":"**`M₆(n) > 0` for `n ≥ 3`**: `(3n−8)²` is a perfect square, positive since `3n−8 ≥ 1 > 0`, and\n`n(n−1)(n−2) > 0`. Manifest perfect-square certificate for the sixth even hook-power moment. Together\nwith `threeM4_pos` this is the first proved positivity in the covariance-kernel epic (`qou-x631`)\nbeyond the `k ≤ 7` `decide` instances. It settles the EVEN half of the moment skeleton; the odd-`k`\nmoments are non-polynomial and remain empirical, and this does **not** prove A2 (whose weight `ln` is\nconcave — a global argument is still required). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.threeM4_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.threeM4_pos","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L356-L366","doc":"**`M₄(n) > 0` for `n ≥ 3`** (stated as `3·M₄ > 0`, whence `M₄ = 3·M₄/3 > 0`): after the positive\n`n(n−1)(n−2)` the cofactor `5(3n−8)` is positive past its root `8/3 < 3`. Manifest linear-past-root\ncertificate for the fourth even hook-power moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.M6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.M6","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L352-L354","doc":"`M₆(n) = 7·n(n−1)(n−2)·(3n−8)²` — the sixth even hook-power moment (already integer-coefficient;\nexact polynomial `[0, 896, −2016, 1582, −525, 63]` in `n⁰..n⁵`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.threeM4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.threeM4","kind":"def","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L348-L350","doc":"`3·M₄(n) = 5·n(n−1)(n−2)·(3n−8)` — the integer form of the fourth even hook-power moment\n`M₄(n) = n(n−1)(n−2)/3 · 5(3n−8)` (so `M₄(n) = threeM4 n / 3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_pos_of_le_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_pos_of_le_eight","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L309-L328","doc":"**`M₁ > 0` — the first odd hook-power moment, Lean-verified base cases `3 ≤ k ≤ 8`** (`decide`).\nThe `(k!)²`-scaled Plancherel covariance `scaledCov k (Σ□ h) (Σ□ c²) = (k!)²·Cov_Planch(Σ□ h, Σ□ c²)`\n(same sign as `M₁`, since `(k!)² > 0`) is **strictly positive** for every `3 ≤ k ≤ 8`. Machine-checked\nover the full partition / SYT-dimension / hook / content machinery. (`k = 8` decides in ≈40 s cold;\nthe `k ≤ 8` range matches `hookSqSum_eq_contentSq_add_sq_card_of_le_eight` above.)\n\nThis certifies the **finite base** of the one-sided reduction of the all-`n` conjecture\n`M₁(n) > 0 ⟸ (exact `M₁>0` for small `n`) ∧ (κ_n ≥ κ for `n ≥ 13`)` (bean `qou-k5r5`), where\n`κ_n = M₁/n^{5/2} → κ = 128/(225π²)` (derived). Unlike the **even** moments (`threeM4_pos`, `M6_pos`,\nexact polynomials with manifest-positive factorisations), `M₁` is **non-polynomial**, so its all-`n`\npositivity is **open**: the remaining content is the *sign* `κ_n → κ` from above, a **second-order\nPlancherel-fluctuation** statement whose asymptotic order is **undetermined** at reachable `n` — the\nedge (Tracy–Widom) contributes at relative order `n^{-2/3}` (a valid scaling estimate) and a bulk CLT\ncorrection at `n^{-1/2}`, but the measured effective exponent of `κ_n − κ` is still rising (`≈ 0.25 →\n0.36` over `n = 40 … 64`, not converged), so edge vs bulk **cannot be ranked**. Not settled here; see\n`docs/audits/2026-08-23-covariance-kernel-M1-correction-bulk-not-edge.md`. Exact `Fraction`\ncomputation independently verifies `M₁ > 0` for all `n ≤ 67`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_eq_cov_rowSq_contentSq_of_le_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_eq_cov_rowSq_contentSq_of_le_five","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L289-L305","doc":"**`M₁` as a content-spread covariance and as a row-length covariance** (Lean-verified `k ≤ 5`,\n`decide`), the `(k!)²`-scaled chain\n`Cov(Σh, Σh²) = Cov(Σh, Σc²) = Cov(Σ_i λ_i², Σc²)`. The first equality is the constant-shift from\n`hookSqSum_eq_contentSq_add_sq_card_of_le_eight`; the second is today's antidiagonal reformulation\n(`docs/audits/2026-08-21-covariance-kernel-M1-antidiagonal-reformulation.md`): via\n`Σ_□ h = n_λ + n_{λ'} + n` and `Σ_i C(λ_i,2) = (Σ_i λ_i² − n)/2`, the first odd moment equals the\ncovariance of the **squared row lengths** with the **squared contents**. Both `Σ_i λ_i²` and `Σ_□ c²`\nare second moments (of parts, of contents); `Σ_i λ_i² ∉` the shifted-symmetric algebra, which is why\n`M₁` is non-polynomial. This is verified computationally to `n ≤ 24`\n(`wlambda_covariance_epic_M1_antidiagonal_reformulation.py`,\n`wlambda_covariance_epic_A2_odd_moment_structure.py`); `decide` machine-checks it for `k ≤ 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSqSum_eq_contentSq_add_sq_card_of_le_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSqSum_eq_contentSq_add_sq_card_of_le_eight","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L281-L287","doc":"**Per-partition hook-square / content-square identity** `Σ_□ h(□)² = Σ_□ c(□)² + |λ|²`, verified\nfor all `λ ⊢ k`, `k ≤ 8` (`decide`). Classical (`Σh² = Σc² + n²`); the exact reason `M₁` can be\nwritten against `contentSq` rather than `hookSqSum`: at fixed `n` the two differ by the `λ`-independent\nconstant `n²`, so they have the same Plancherel covariance with any statistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.rowSqSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.rowSqSum","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L278-L279","doc":"Sum of squared row lengths `Σ_i λ_i²` (a `List ℕ` power sum), cast to `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_transpose_identity_scaled_of_le_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.m1_transpose_identity_scaled_of_le_five","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L264-L276","doc":"**First-odd-moment transpose identity** (Lean-verified, `k ≤ 5`, `decide`), the `(k!)²`-scaled form\nof `M₁ = Cov_Planch(Σ_□ h, Σ_□ h²) = 2·Cov_Planch(n_λ, Σ_□ c²)`:\n`scaledCov k (Σh) (Σh²) = 2·scaledCov k n_λ (Σc²)`. This is the odd-`k=1` companion of the *even*-moment\nresult: unlike the even moments (exact polynomials, positivity proved — `threeM4_pos`, `M6_pos`), `M₁`\nis non-polynomial, but the hook-sum decomposition (`hookSum_eq_nLambda_add_conj_add_card_of_le_seven`)\ntogether with Plancherel transpose-invariance collapses it to twice a *content*-spread covariance\n`Cov_Planch(n_λ, Σc²)` — the same difficulty class as the open kernel `Cov_Planch(f^λ, Σc²) ≤ 0`. The\nidentity is verified computationally to `n ≤ 14` (`wlambda_covariance_epic_A2_odd_moment_structure.py`);\nthis `decide` machine-checks it over the full partition/dimension machinery for `k ≤ 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSum_eq_nLambda_add_conj_add_card_of_le_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSum_eq_nLambda_add_conj_add_card_of_le_seven","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L251-L262","doc":"**Hook-sum decomposition** (Lean-verified, `λ ⊢ k`, `k ≤ 7`, `decide`):\n`Σ_□ h(□) = n_λ + n_{λ'} + |λ|`, splitting the total hook length into the row-content `n_λ`, the\ncolumn-content `n_{λ'} = n_λ` of the transpose, and the cell count `|λ|`. This is the algebraic key to\nthe first-odd-moment **transpose identity** `M₁ = 2·Cov_Planch(n_λ, Σ_□ c(□)²)` (companion probe/audit\n`wlambda_covariance_epic_A2_odd_moment_structure`): substituting `Σ_□ h = n_λ + n_{λ'} + |λ|` into\n`Cov_Planch(Σ_□ h, Σ_□ c²)`, the `|λ|` term is constant (zero covariance) and transpose-invariance of\nPlancherel measure together with the conjugation-symmetry of `contentSq`\n(`contentSq_conj_invariant_of_le_six`) equate the `n_λ` and `n_{λ'}` covariances — collapsing the sum\nto `2·Cov_Planch(n_λ, Σc²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.omega3_conj_invariant_of_le_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.omega3_conj_invariant_of_le_six","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L243-L249","doc":"`ω₃` is conjugation-invariant on `λ ⊢ k`, `k ≤ 6` (`decide`): `omega3 k (conj λ) = omega3 k λ`\n(immediate from `contentSq_conj_invariant_of_le_six`, since `ω₃` only shifts `contentSq` by a\n`λ`-independent constant). This symmetry pairs the kernel summands `(f^λ)³ω₃(λ)` into conjugate pairs\n(except at self-conjugate `λ`), the structural obstruction to any local sign certificate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.contentSq_conj_invariant_of_le_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.contentSq_conj_invariant_of_le_six","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L230-L241","doc":"Content-square is **conjugation-invariant** — verified for all `λ ⊢ k`, `k ≤ 6` (`decide`):\n`contentSq (conj λ) = contentSq λ`. Reason: the transpose bijection on cells `(i,j) ↦ (j,i)` sends the\ncontent `j−i` to `i−j`, and `(i−j)² = (j−i)²`. Consequence: `ω₃` is conjugation-symmetric, hence\n**U-shaped** (large at both the row and column extremes, small in the balanced middle) — which is\nexactly why no monotone / FKG / comonotone certificate for the kernel can work. The general (`∀`\nsorted `l`) statement follows from the sorted-List transpose bijection\n`cellSum (conj l) f = cellSum l (fun i j => f j i)` (via `len (conj l) = l.headD 0`,\n`conj l |>.getD r 0 = #{i : l.getD i 0 > r}`, and the staircase equivalence\n`c < (conj l).getD r 0 ↔ r < l.getD c 0`); that infra is not yet built here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_twenty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_twenty","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L208-L228","doc":"**Extended machine-checked base for the dim²-weighted vanishing: `k ≤ 20`.** Extends\n`secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_seven` over the same range as the kernel base\n`kernelValue_nonpos_of_le_twenty`. Unlike the kernel conjecture, this identity is **not**\nconjectural — it is `k!·E_Planch[ω₃] = 0`, exact for every `k` (the identity coefficient of\n`Σ_i X_i²` in the Jucys–Murphy calculus is `C(k,2)`); what the `decide` supplies is a certified\nfloor pending the general character-orthogonality proof, which needs the JM-eigenvalue ⇒\nPlancherel-mean bridge (Sₙ representation-theory infrastructure, not yet in the corpus).\n\n**Superseded 2026-08-23 — the general-`k` proof exists.**\n`SecondMomentKernelVanishes.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero` proves this for **every** `k`, with no\nbound and no `decide`.  The sentence above — *\"pending the general character-orthogonality proof,\nwhich needs the JM-eigenvalue ⇒ Plancherel-mean bridge (Sₙ representation-theory infrastructure,\nnot yet in the corpus)\"* — named exactly what was missing, and it has since landed: that bridge is\nIdentity (ii) (`OVTopAssembly.identityB_general`, transported to the list model by\n`PlancherelSnDataGeneral`), built from the three inputs the `k ≤ 7` docstring lists.  This lemma\nremains the cheaper route inside its range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_nonpos_of_le_twenty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_nonpos_of_le_twenty","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L193-L204","doc":"**Extended machine-checked base: the kernel conjecture holds for `3 ≤ k ≤ 20`** (kernel\n`decide` over the full partition/hook/dimension machinery; `maxRecDepth`/`maxHeartbeats` raised\nfor the larger enumerations — elaboration limits, not a change in trust: the kernel still checks\nevery step). Extends the `k ≤ 7` base to cover, in particular, the whole `k ≤ 14` range on which\nthe two open pincer legs (`Cov₂(ln f, ω₃) ≤ 0` and the interpolation remainder bound) have been\nnumerically verified — so any future effective-constant proof of those legs closes the conjecture\ndown to a floor the kernel has already certified. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_nonpos_of_le_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_nonpos_of_le_seven","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L185-L189","doc":"The covariance-kernel conjecture is **Lean-verified for `3 ≤ k ≤ 7`** (kernel `decide`), a\nmachine-checked base for the open general statement below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_base_values_to_fourteen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_base_values_to_fourteen","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L175-L183","doc":"Extended Lean-kernel-verified base **values** `k = 8..14` — the exact integers, cross-checking\nthe Python pipeline (`wlambda_covariance_kernel_frontier.py`) against the kernel evaluator over\nthe same partition/hook machinery. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_base_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue_base_values","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L167-L171","doc":"Lean-kernel-verified base **values** of `kernelValue` (checked by `decide` over the full\npartition/hook machinery, grounding the otherwise Python-only verification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero_of_le_seven","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L138-L165","doc":"**The dim²-weighted 3-cycle content-spread total VANISHES** (Lean-verified, `3 ≤ k ≤ 7`):\n`Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)² ω₃(λ) = 0`. This is `k!·E_Planch[ω₃] = 0` (the Plancherel content mean is `C(k,2)`) —\nan **exact** identity, not conjectural. It isolates the open kernel as the *first-order response to the\nextra dimension factor*: `cov(k) = Σ (f^λ)³ ω₃ = k!·Cov_Planch(f^λ, ω₃)`, a genuine dimension-tilt\ncovariance (Ivanov–Olshanski Prop 5.1; the `dim³` weight has one surplus `dim` beyond column\northogonality, so — unlike this `dim²` total — it lies outside the polynomial-function algebra `A`).\n\n**Why `3 ≤ k ≤ 7` is a Lean artifact, and exactly what would remove it.** The identity holds for\nevery `k`, and the shortest route is Jucys–Murphy rather than Prop 5.1. Writing `X_i = Σ_{j<i} (i j)`,\nthe JM theorem gives that `Σ_i X_i²` is **central**, acting on the irrep `λ` by the eigenvalue\n`Σ_□ c(□)²` (each standard-tableau basis vector picks up `c(□)²` box by box). Expanding the square,\n`(i j)² = 1` contributes `C(k,2)·1`, and every cross term `(i j)(i l)` with `j ≠ l` is a **3-cycle**:\n\n  `Σ_i X_i² = C(k,2)·1 + (3-cycle class sum)`.\n\nReading off eigenvalues, `Σ_□ c(□)² = C(k,2) + const·ω^λ_{(3)}`, so\n`Σ_λ (f^λ)² ω₃(λ) ∝ Σ_λ f^λ χ^λ(3-cyc) = 0` by **column orthogonality** — the whole identity is that\none vanishing, with no asymptotics anywhere.\n\nLifting `interval_cases … decide` to a general-`k` proof therefore needs exactly three imports from\nthe Specht/`S_n` epic (`sp00`), and nothing else: (i) the JM elements with their content\neigenvalues, (ii) centrality of `Σ_i X_i^m`, (iii) column orthogonality `Σ_λ f^λ χ^λ(σ) = 0` for\n`σ ≠ 1`. That is the concrete `sp00` dependency for this lemma; the `k ≤ 7` bound is a `decide`\nbudget, not a mathematical frontier. (Recorded 2026-08-15 while attacking `qou-v8t7`; the reduction\nis standard, the point here is naming the three inputs so `sp00` can be aimed at them.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.secondMomentKernel","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L134-L136","doc":"Second-moment (dim²-weighted) content-spread total `Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)² · ω₃(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4WeightedSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4WeightedSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**Sum-level affine identity (sorry-free).** `Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)³ R₄(λ) = 3·kernelValue(k) − k·cubeSum(k)`.\nThe `R₄`-weighted total differs from the covariance kernel only by the affine cube-sum term `k·cubeSum`.\nConsequence: adding the constant `−k` to `ω₃` shifts the raw weighted sum but leaves the *covariance*\n`Cov_Planch(f^λ, ·)` unchanged, so the free-cumulant form `Cov_Planch(f^λ, R₄) ≤ 0` is the **same\ninequality** as the content form `Cov_Planch(f^λ, ω₃) ≤ 0` — `R₄` is not an independent handle on the\nopen kernel. (Phase-2 finding, `qou-x631`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4_sum_affine_list","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4_sum_affine_list","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L107-L120","doc":"General list form of the affine linearity: for any list `L` of diagrams,\n`Σ_l (f^l)³ · (3·ω₃(l) − k) = 3·Σ_l (f^l)³·ω₃(l) − k·Σ_l (f^l)³`. Sorry-free (induction on `L`);\nit exhibits exactly how the `−k` shift enters at the **summed** level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4WeightedSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4WeightedSum","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L103-L105","doc":"The `R₄`-weighted total `Σ_{λ ⊢ k} (f^λ)³ · R₄(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.cubeSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.cubeSum","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L100-L101","doc":"Cube-of-dimension total `Σ_{λ ⊢ k} (f^λ)³` (the `(f^λ)³`-biasing normaliser). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4Value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.r4Value","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The 4th free cumulant `R₄` of the transition measure of `λ`, in Biane's normalisation\n`Σ̂₃ = R₄ + R₂` with `R₂ = k`: `R₄(λ) = 3·ω₃(λ) − k`. This is an **exactly affine** relabelling of\nthe content spread `ω₃` — verified `E_Planch[R₄] = −k` computationally\n(`wlambda_covariance_epic_phase2.py`, `k ≤ 8`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.omega3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.omega3","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The 3-cycle class-sum eigenvalue on the irrep `λ`: `ω₃(λ) = Σ_□ c(□)² − C(k,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.kernelValue","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L85-L89","doc":"The elementary content form of the covariance kernel value at level `k`:\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ k} (f^λ)³ · (Σ_□ c(□)² − C(k,2))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.scaledCov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.scaledCov","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L77-L83","doc":"`(k!)²`-scaled Plancherel covariance `(k!)²·Cov_Planch(X, Y)` of two `λ`-statistics at level `k`,\nkept over `ℤ` (the `dim²/k!` Plancherel weights cleared to integers):\n`k!·Σ_λ (f^λ)² X(λ)Y(λ) − (Σ_λ (f^λ)² X(λ))(Σ_λ (f^λ)² Y(λ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSqSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSqSum","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L70-L75","doc":"Sum of squared hook lengths `Σ_□ h(□)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.nLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.nLambda","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L66-L68","doc":"Row-content statistic `n_λ = Σ_i i·λ_i` (0-indexed rows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookSum","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L59-L64","doc":"Sum of hook lengths over all cells: `Σ_□ h(□)`, `h(i,j) = λ_i + λ'_j − i − j − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.sytDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.sytDim","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L56-L57","doc":"Hook-length dimension `f^λ = |λ|! / ∏_□ h(□)` (number of standard Young tableaux). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.hookProd","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L49-L54","doc":"Product of hook lengths over all cells: hook`(i,j) = λ_i + λ'_j − i − j − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.conj","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Conjugate partition: `λ'_j = #{ i : λ_i > j }`, for `j = 0 .. λ_0 − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.contentSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.contentSq","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L40-L43","doc":"Content-square sum `Σ_□ c(□)²`, `c(i,j) = j − i`, over cells of the diagram `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.partsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.partsOf","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L37-L38","doc":"Partitions of `n` (as weakly-decreasing lists of positive parts). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.partsFuel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernel.partsFuel","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramKernel.lean#L28-L35","doc":"Enumerate partitions of `n` with parts `≤ maxPart`, structural on `fuel` (take `fuel = n`).\nEach partition is a weakly-decreasing `List ℕ` of positive parts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}